---

Why this and not MIT.

PhotoFlow is a portfolio project that may also be offered commercially. A
permissive licence would allow anyone to run it as a competing service, and
that decision cannot be undone once made: code released under MIT stays
available under MIT for everyone who already has a copy.

A source-available notice costs nothing for the purpose this repository mostly
serves — being read — while leaving the commercial question open.

If the intent later changes to genuine open source, replacing this file with a
standard licence text is a one-file change. Going the other direction is not.
